    commonErrors: "Typical failures: assuming generic guidance is a legal limit; omitting receptor or abnormal-condition assessment; beginning before approval or briefing; unclear accountability; weak or unrepresentative monitoring; outdated documents; incomplete attachments or traceability; delayed escalation; closing actions without field verification; and failing to reassess after a change.",
    fieldExample: "At a site activity involving daily walkdown, briefing, control checks, intervention, escalation, coaching and evidence-based closeout, the supervisor and Environmental Officer review the current approval conditions, map the relevant receptors, brief the crew, inspect preventive controls and confirm the response route. A defect, complaint, abnormal result or incident is recorded promptly; the affected work is made safe, the responsible lead is notified, corrective action is assigned and effectiveness is checked before formal closure.",
    checklist: "Scope and definition understood; sources/pathways/receptors identified; current UAE/emirate and permit obligations verified; risk/aspect assessment and approved method current; hierarchy of controls applied; competent owner and approver named; workers/contractors briefed; controls and equipment inspected; monitoring/trigger response ready where applicable; emergency and notification route known; records/attachments controlled; deviations corrected and effectiveness verified.",
    interview: "Be prepared to explain: what Environmental Leadership and Supervisor Field Duties means; purpose and applicability; sources, pathways and receptors; how you verify current UAE federal, emirate and permit conditions; aspects/impacts and risk significance; hierarchy of controls; competent roles; records and approval sequence; monitoring/inspection frequency basis; stop-work and escalation conditions; practical site example; common failure and corrective action. State the source, jurisdiction, revision and applicability for any numerical criterion instead of guessing.",
  ),
];
